3(x + 2) + 4x\n$$\n\n \n\nOur first step is to distribute the $3$ over each of the terms in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t3(x + 2) + 4x &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t3\\cdot x + 3\\cdot 2 + 4x &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t(3x) + (6) + 4x &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t3x +6 + 4x &\n\t}\n$$\n\nThe second and final step is to collect the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t3x + 6 + 4x &= \\\n\t\t(3x + 4x) + 6 &= \\\n\t\t7x + 6\n\t}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056008 #edb/ref 1065 8024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056008 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "4f6f52d9-c069-5009-ae28-6eb58953a5cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056008 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
